{"id":"dar-chensal","name":"Dar Chensal","type":"character","aliases":["Dar","guilt"],"description":"A Jeskai Arbiter Twin born in the darkness of night, who announces guilt.","pages":2,"first_seen":"2014-10-15","last_seen":"2014-10-15","description_citations":[{"source":"mtg-wiki","official":false,"publisher":"MTG Wiki contributors","work":"Kela and Dar Chensal","series":"MTG Wiki","authors":[],"date":"","url":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Kela_and_Dar_Chensal","link":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Kela_and_Dar_Chensal","archived":null,"license":"CC BY-NC-SA 4.0","text":"\"Kela and Dar Chensal\". MTG Wiki contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0."}],"bio":null,"timeline":[{"id":"kela-and-dar-chensal-e0","era":{"date":"2014-09-26","era":"ktk","label":"Khans of Tarkir"},"summary":"Kela and Dar are called to Jigme Village to judge the theft of nine baskets of apples; Elder Ngabo brings them before Lotse Taring.","participants":["kela-chensal","dar-chensal","elder-ngabo","lotse-taring"],"location":"jigme-village","importance":"minor","page":"wiki/kela-and-dar-chensal","order":2087,"story_date":"","storyline":"Khans of Tarkir","source":"mtg-wiki","paragraph":2,"quote":"Kela and Dar were called to Jigme Village to adjudicate a case of nine baskets of apples that had been stolen.","link":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Kela_and_Dar_Chensal#:~:text=Kela%20and%20Dar%20were,that%20had%20been%20stolen.","citation":{"source":"mtg-wiki","official":false,"publisher":"MTG Wiki contributors","work":"Kela and Dar Chensal","series":"MTG Wiki","authors":[],"date":"","url":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Kela_and_Dar_Chensal","link":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Kela_and_Dar_Chensal#:~:text=Kela%20and%20Dar%20were,that%20had%20been%20stolen.","archived":null,"license":"CC BY-NC-SA 4.0","text":"\"Kela and Dar Chensal\", section \"History\". MTG Wiki contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0."}},{"id":"kela-and-dar-chensal-e1","era":{"date":"2014-09-26","era":"ktk","label":"Khans of Tarkir"},"summary":"Dar lights the lamp of guilt, ending the trial